<section class="phero"><img class="phero-img" src="/assets/img/photos/review-meeting.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/review-meeting-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/review-meeting.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><div class="wrap"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span><a href="/claim-tools-nebraska/">Claim tools</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span><span aria-current="page">Appraisal Readiness Check</span></nav><p class="tag">Free checklist</p><h1>Appraisal Readiness Check</h1><p class="lede">Appraisal works best with a complete file. Answer ten questions to see how ready you are and what to gather before making a demand.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec toolsec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Appraisal readiness check</span><i>10 questions · about 2 minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get the coverage position in writing. Appraisal values a covered loss; it does not decide coverage."><span>Has the insurer accepted that the loss is covered?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask for the full line-item estimate, not just the payment letter."><span>Do you have the carrier’s complete, itemized estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Get a detailed, itemized estimate from a qualified contractor or estimator."><span>Do you have a contractor’s or independent estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Photograph every slope, elevation and room, plus soft metals and outbuildings."><span>Are there date-stamped photos of every damaged area?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Pin down the storm date with weather records or news reports."><span>Do you know the date of loss and the storm that caused it?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Find the appraisal condition in your policy and note any deadlines."><span>Have you read the appraisal clause in your own policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Tarp, board up or dry out the property and keep every receipt."><span>Have you made temporary repairs and saved receipts?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Run the award gap estimator to see whether fees would eat the recovery."><span>Is the dispute larger than a few thousand dollars?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Use the claim calendar builder, and talk to an attorney if a suit deadline is close."><span>Are you sure no policy deadline has passed?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Send a written supplement request with your evidence first; it may close the gap."><span>Have you asked the adjuster in writing to reconsider?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li></ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn line small" data-reset>Start over</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="gauge"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" class="g-bg"/><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" class="g-fg" data-o="arc"/></svg><div><b data-o="score">–</b><small>readiness</small></div></div>
      <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
      <p class="count">Answered: <b data-o="count">0 / 10</b></p>
      <p class="todo-h">To do before you demand appraisal</p>
      <ul class="todo" data-o="todo"><li>Nothing flagged yet.</li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="disclaim">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>Why readiness matters</h2>
<p>The appraisal award is binding on the amount of loss. If you demand appraisal before you have the carrier’s full estimate, your own estimate and good photos, you risk locking in a number that leaves damage out.</p>
<h2>How the score works</h2>
<p>Questions are weighted. Coverage acceptance and having the carrier’s itemized estimate count most, because appraisal cannot work without them. Each “No” adds a specific task to your list.</p>
<h2>After you score</h2>
<p>A strong score means it may be time for a professional review of the dollar gap. A lower score gives you a checklist. Either way, our <a href="/appraisal-services-nebraska/carrier-estimate-review/">carrier estimate review</a> is a sensible next step.</p>

<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does a high score mean I will win?</summary><div class="a"><p>No. It means your file has the basics an appraisal panel expects. Outcomes depend on the evidence.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is my answer list saved?</summary><div class="a"><p>No. Everything stays in your browser.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I retake it?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. Use Start over at any time.</p></div></details></div>
